# Safety skills

`/careful`, `/freeze`, and `/guard` are opt-in. Cursor hooks in `.cursor/hooks.json` enforce them only after the matching skill writes state.

- `/careful` — warn (and hard-deny catastrophic shapes) before `rm -rf`, `DROP TABLE`, force-push, `git reset --hard`. Touches `$GSTACK_HOME/careful-active`.
- `/freeze` — block Write/StrReplace outside the chosen directory. Writes `$GSTACK_HOME/freeze-dir.txt`.
- `/guard` — both. `/unfreeze` clears the freeze file.

Even when hooks are idle, confirm with the user before recursive deletes, force-pushes to the default branch, or production-data destruction.
